@startuml M6-Index-Activity

' Index operation activity flow: from raw documents to searchable index
' Shows all steps: extract text -> normalize -> tokenize -> stem -> count
' Includes MapReduce jobs and statistics calculation

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam activityBorderColor #333
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam arrowColor #333
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - Index Operation Activity Flow

start
:Load documents
from M4 Store;
:Initialize inverted
index & statistics;

repeat
  :Get document
  from batch;
  
  partition "Text Processing" {
    :Extract README
    content;
    :Normalize text
    (lowercase, remove special chars);
    :Tokenize
    (split into words);
    :Stem words
    (Porter Stemmer);
    :Generate n-grams
    (bigrams, trigrams);
  }
  
  :Count term
  frequencies;
  
  :Add to
  inverted index;
  
  :Update statistics:
  - term frequency (TF)
  - document frequency (DF);
  
  note right
    Inverted Index:
    term -> [docId1, docId2, ...]
    (posting lists)
    
    TF: [term][docId] = count
    DF: [term] = #docs
  end note
  
repeat while (More documents?)

:Finalize index;

partition "MapReduce Jobs (Optional)" {
  :Job 1: Calculate IDF
  (log N / DF);
  
  :Job 2: Compute
  Document Length
  (total word count);
  
  :Job 3: Run PageRank
  (repo importance);
}

:Store inverted index
(Posting lists);
:Store TF statistics
(Document frequencies);
:Store DF statistics
(Inverse doc freq);
:Store PageRank scores;

:Index complete;
:Report stats:
- total terms indexed
- total postings
- index size (MB);

stop

note right
  Performance targets:
  - Index rate: ~2000 terms/sec
  - Total index time: 2-5 seconds
    for 100 repos (~10,000 terms)
  
  MapReduce (optional):
  - Enables parallel processing
  - For large datasets (1000+ repos)
  - Distributes work across M1-M5 nodes
end note

@enduml
